{% comment %}
  The cart drawer's own loading spinner.

  It is a separate snippet from 'loading-spinner' because the two produce
  different markup and both are needed: Dawn's emits `.loading__spinner` and is
  used by nine other components in this theme, while the ported cart is written
  around `.loading-overlay` — the drawer's stylesheet positions
  `.cart-item__actions .loading-overlay`, and cart.js's enableLoading() finds
  the right row with `querySelectorAll('.loading-overlay')[line - 1]`. Rendering
  Dawn's shape here left both looking at nothing, so a line being updated or
  removed gave no feedback at all.

  Usage:
  {%- render 'cart-loading-spinner' -%}
{% endcomment %}

<div class="loading-overlay hidden">
  <div class="loading-overlay__spinner">
    {% render 'icon', icon: 'spinner' %}
  </div>
</div>
